      "text": "This route reveals Uruguay through four very different stories. Begin in Montevideo, with the Rambla waterfront, the old town and Uruguayan cuisine. Then visit the vineyards and old cellar of Bodega Spinoglio. From the capital, head west to San Javier, founded by Russian settlers, and Fray Bentos, with its industrial heritage. The programme ends in Colonia del Sacramento, where Portuguese and Spanish architecture stand side by side along cobbled streets.",
